# Research Drive — Figma implementation rules

## Component map

- Shell: `src/main.jsx` (`App`, nav sections, view routing)
- Styles: `src/drive-visual.css` (desk tokens), `src/styles.css` (legacy)
- Data: `src/driveTree.js`, `src/profileDrive.js`
- Comparison board: `docs/status/generated/research-drive-oss-comparison.html`

## Design tokens (use these — never hardcode hex in new UI)

From `drive-visual.css`:

- Surfaces: `--nav`, `--surface`, `--surface2`, `--surface3`
- Text: `--text`, `--muted`, `--faint`
- Accent: `--accent`, `--accent2`
- Lines: `--line`, `--line2`
- Spacing: `--space-*`, radius: `--radius-md`

## IA (signed direction — do not regress)

**Internal:** Home, Recent, Starred, Drive, Cluster  
**Procure:** Discover → Browse (HF-style, not built yet)  
**Tools:** Chat (full page), Activity  

- One L1 per screen (list, map, chat thread)
- Inspector = Details only on browse; Chat is not a rail tab
- Procure CTAs: header Chat, Discover footnote, Chat page — not duplicate cards on Drive

## Figma MCP workflow (required when implementing from Figma)

1. `get_design_context` + `get_screenshot` for target node
2. Map to existing classes (`rd-catalog-table`, `rd-page-bar`, `yzu-sidebar`, etc.)
3. Validate against `node scripts/rd_oss_comparison_page.mjs` captures
4. Run `npm run build` + Playwright `e2e/desk.spec.js`

## OSS parity targets

| Surface | Steal from | Not done until |
|---------|------------|----------------|
| Drive | Google Drive list + HF dataset rows | Browse route with Overview/Files/Schema |
| Discover | HF hub search + filters | Rec grid + drill to Browse |
| Cluster | Cite-Agent Coverage map | Domain brief, gap cards, promote timeline |
| Chat | Cite-Agent `/chat` | Workbench layout, not dropped procure card |

## Do not

- Re-add folder tree rail on Drive
- Stack Smart Procure card above catalog list
- Use Source tab in inspector (use Chat nav)
- Claim visual sign-off without screenshot review at 1440×900
